## Inputs for the paper's theory and cost sections (reported, not verdicts)

- `runs/round8/test_heads.out` (V 600, d 16, C 24, 500 random h): log-prob rank flat / class-bias / two-level = 18 / 41 / 41, checked bounds 18 / 41 / 41; exact greedy 64/64, 1.75 clusters expanded on average (of 24); sampling TV 0.0096 (200k samples).
- Bug (documentation): test_heads.py checks d + 2 (flat log-probs, bias + normaliser) and d + C + 1 (class-bias, hier); the heads.py docstring says d + 1 and d + C, i.e. it counts logits, not log-probs.
- Head share of training FLOPs at ~600M-parameter GPT shapes (f = 4d, T = 1024, model.flops_per_token's formula):
  - d 1024, 48 layers, V 50,257 (655M params): flat 7.3%, two-level 1.9% (head FLOPs ratio 0.245)
  - d 1024, 48 layers, V 131,072 (738M params): flat 17.0%, two-level 1.9% (head FLOPs ratio 0.094)
